NTRE implementations
====================

This directory contains the NTRE KEM implementation packages.

Layout
------

- `Reference_Implementation/`
  Portable ISO C99 reference implementations for `NTRE-128`, `NTRE-256`,
  and `NTRE-512`.

- `Optimized_Implementation/`
  x86_64 AVX2-oriented implementations for `NTRE-128`, `NTRE-256`, and
  `NTRE-512`.  These packages keep the same NGCC KEM API as the reference
  implementations.  The current optimized code uses the documented optimized
  build profile and an AVX2 assembly layer for small polynomial arithmetic
  hot paths.  NTT, inverse NTT, base multiplication, packing, CBD, and mod-2
  decode still use the audited C code path.

Each instance provides:

- `KEM_AlgorithmInstance.c` and `KEM_AlgorithmInstance.h`
- NGCC fixed support files: `KAT_KEM.c`, `auxfunc.*`, `drng.*`
- NTRE-specific arithmetic and symmetric-code files under `src/`
- `Makefile`
- `test/`

Build
-----

From an instance directory:

```sh
make clean all
make test
make kat
```

Some Makefiles only build the test binary when `make test` is invoked from the
instance directory; run the produced test executable if the Makefile does not
execute it automatically.

Performance Records
-------------------

Repository-level performance records are stored in `../Benchmark_Results/`.
The benchmark script `../Benchmark_Results/run_ntre_benchmarks.sh` measures all
three NTRE instances through the NGCC `kem_*` API and records both:

- NGCC document profile: reference `gcc -O2` versus optimized `gcc -O3` with
  AVX2, LTO, native tuning, and frame-pointer omission.
- Same-flags sanity profile: both implementations built with the optimized
  flags, to separate compiler-option effects from source-level differences.

Generated Files
---------------

The following are build or generated test artifacts and should not be kept in
the source package:

- `bin/`
- `output/`
- `test/test_ntre`
- object files and other compiler outputs

Test vectors intended for delivery should live outside this source tree, for
example in the repository-level `Test_Vectors/` directory.
